WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.942
This query displays order timestamps using two time zones.

00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:10.422
AT TIME ZONE America slash New York gives an Eastern local clock representation.

00:00:10.422 --> 00:00:13.832
AT TIME ZONE UTC gives a UTC clock representation.

00:00:13.832 --> 00:00:18.782
Run the query and compare the displayed times.

00:00:18.782 --> 00:00:24.322
The underlying event instant is the same; only the clock representation changes.

00:00:24.322 --> 00:00:30.422
Time zones matter whenever events from different locations need to be compared on one timeline.

00:00:30.422 --> 00:00:38.152
Store instants in a consistent form, often using TIMESTAMPTZ, and convert to local time for presentation.

00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:43.967
Do not permanently rewrite an instant just because a report needs to display it in a local zone.
